{"posts":[{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1226","t":"Away\n\nHi Everyone My compression homework. From what I can understand Cps are a flagging area. In a bullish flag the cp will go down, consuming supply therefore making possible a move up on return. With a bearish flag you can see a CP going up while consuming demand, making it possible for the price to easily go down on return. That's why you will find poles and FLs on the left of a compressed area. Help and comments welcome!","a":"corsica","d":"","n":"#1226","p":50,"im":["0ae92577e4e9f892d1e08cd818be588fb5658083","3a475cdbe89bdbff23c8b7d3e970ca69dd71901d","80195818f8c721ee8e548c3d94ba51e72fc9a30c","a13519b4adcc4cbdf6d553ed0f60b17ecfdc4f86","1bf49a11011a027b654920170a807a9b3824e947","68ed2be3f22195f369547c053897a3531c241998"],"m":1226},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1227","t":"Away\n\na few more","a":"corsica","d":"","n":"#1227","p":50,"im":["1a214f6d344061587581e9d84741f9fa94093fd3","16aaa6cf7d37bc09a24d635afd37ebee3ddf6936","1e25f92a94835c93ec378bc6559899fcc9af1074","893258a31f3987050008a341562314edf321e76d","a11936d7850204a740424548895fa9ffb959e739"],"m":1227},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1228","t":"Away\n\nAnd a last set","a":"corsica","d":"","n":"#1228","p":50,"im":["bd812411a7db77c0444e01ea7db8e0389ecd132c","a7c5996e1422cb60508d19fc4a4b709a608c991a","06c91bce5aec86c166f15214f1a2d6ffa29f9003","a7e4cd4e7965c1258f06a0a7a88c6a854d3d10b7","a71bed0eab55c7c66531b96f7cc0bf9e74667f5e"],"m":1228},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1229","t":"Some CP observations NZDUSD daily:","a":"moogroo","d":"","n":"#1229","p":50,"im":["a9f6176415166e31bd3b51ed5e74411496083866"],"m":1229},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1230","t":"EURUSD currently reacting to a Daily demand. 5min chart...","a":"moogroo","d":"","n":"#1230","p":50,"im":["6ba1917cf188034db0f03fbe82b3659a2fddd380"],"m":1230},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1231","t":"This is the continuation of the EURUSD chart from the previous post... part 1:\n\npart 2:\n\npart 3: Charting this one during a big news event; Draghi's speech from the ECB.","a":"moogroo","d":"","n":"#1231","p":50,"im":["226354bbec64947e186b4cf14fca0426c933394a","ad8ec61f9c68f169542e19b82bc8e626c80c1b56","0333032b710c301fb25b477b61928a96972d87fd"],"m":1231},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1232","t":"hi guys details in the chart\n\nfull","a":"full","d":"","n":"#1232","p":50,"im":["83350a2ecb94a0a9db2c45f556ebabf7a921f16d"],"m":1232},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1233","t":"full wrote: hi guys details in the chart\n\nGood job mate\n\nMissed mine...","a":"Paraipan","d":"","n":"#1233","p":50,"im":["83350a2ecb94a0a9db2c45f556ebabf7a921f16d","80289cb1665aebb134a2f840d9e246f1cb328514"],"m":1233},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1234","t":"i'm sorry bro.look at decision point origin of the down move (engulf)","a":"full","d":"","n":"#1234","p":50,"im":[],"m":1234},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1235","t":"full wrote: i'm sorry bro.look at decision point origin of the down move (engulf)\n\nGot it, clean orders left unfilled","a":"Paraipan","d":"","n":"#1235","p":50,"im":[],"m":1235},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1236","t":"Moar Homework!\n\narea before releasing to the downside...\n\nHere is the 5min chart zooming in on the price action before the big drop...","a":"moogroo","d":"","n":"#1236","p":50,"im":["9573dd3a45c04e4c9b77131622645b5ee2ee5fb9","d1485dea512cab0f9c1756e18f5213108906d777"],"m":1236},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1237","t":"the best setup","a":"zaindeviana","d":"","n":"#1237","p":50,"im":[],"m":1237},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1238","t":"Hi, Please take a look at my first chart on compression, I couldn't find the download for the document so have just gone by the initial post from IF and what I found on REDSWORD11 thread. Great site with a really good ethos, I really hope that one day I can provide feedback for others and give something back to this community.\n\nAll comments welcome and thanks to Salivan for providing comments on my RBD/DBR homework.","a":"mtom","d":"","n":"#1238","p":50,"im":["9c1b2f1e2024f15ee39ff25d068452d88ab49701"],"m":1238},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1239","t":"Please correct","a":"Shantala","d":"","n":"#1239","p":50,"im":["4fc87f6190b3b176a7c73adda143921f899483cf"],"m":1239},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1240","t":"Shantala wrote: Please correct\n\nMark every cp you find. It's a good start, keep it up","a":"Rakkain","d":"","n":"#1240","p":50,"im":["4fc87f6190b3b176a7c73adda143921f899483cf","6b48ff5d6c4f99bd0b486af33b9da80868d85f52"],"m":1240},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1241","t":"Guys, would it still be considered a compresssion if the demand zones on H4 are revisitted or compressed while the smaller demand zones on H1 aren't compressed? Hope to hear your thoughts.","a":"Enlightenme","d":"","n":"#1241","p":50,"im":["b21eadfa90b8d02cffc00179d777346e366e2a7d"],"m":1241},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1242","t":"Enlightenme wrote:\n\nHi Enlightenme i think it really depends on the scale you are looking at!\n\nFor example if you have a compression in daily time frame toward a true supply, you can see the price strongly pass through the compression in daily, at the same time if you look at lower time frame, for example M15, you can find fresh demand there that stopped the price several times! It's the same for other time frames too","a":"omidfxt","d":"","n":"#1242","p":50,"im":["b21eadfa90b8d02cffc00179d777346e366e2a7d"],"m":1242},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1243","t":"Away\n\nomidfxt wrote:\n\nEnlightenme wrote:\n\nhi omid, so we should difine scales by timeframe, is that true?","a":"alirezat","d":"","n":"#1243","p":50,"im":["b21eadfa90b8d02cffc00179d777346e366e2a7d"],"m":1243},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1244","t":"alirezat wrote: hi omid, so we should difine scales by timeframe, is that true?\n\nYes. i think they are the same things!","a":"omidfxt","d":"","n":"#1244","p":50,"im":[],"m":1244},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1245","t":"Hi Omidfxt I think I misstated my question... so should we expect price to pass through those area (of compression on H4 but not on H1)?\n\nWould it matter if the compression was seen on H1 and not on H4?","a":"Enlightenme","d":"","n":"#1245","p":50,"im":[],"m":1245},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1246","t":"Hi Enlightenme, please see first the first post of this homework and have a good read on the Compression book (Red's work)\n\nIfmyante wrote: Compression is one of the most important signs that price is getting ready to turn.\n\nAs price is rising into Supply, it keeps dropping as it goes, filling the buy orders left at each Demand on the way up, allowing a quick drop through the CP zone when price hits Supply.\n\nThe exact opposite is true for Compression into Demand.\n\nHere is a PDF about Compression www.readthemarket.com/media/pdf/Compression.pdf\n\nHomework\n\nYour question: expect price to pass through? in any timeframe? What works or doesnot on CP-ed area is widely discussed here already. Price Action applies to all timeframes. If you have troubles understanding compression, Go over all the posts in this HW section, Pay attention to words/corrections made by the seniors here, and watch CP webinar by IF. Then you may start doing the HW instructions (pay attention too to the instructions). This will take time, please do not expect to grasp just by skimming and looking at the posts. Learning by doing is best.:)","a":"staurum","d":"","n":"#1246","p":50,"im":["991ea1be359743b6730a5d1b458341dd405d7805"],"m":1246},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1247","t":"Ifmyante wrote: We're starting a new section on the homepage called No-Brainer trades - you'll see it tomorrow.\n\nBut the first chart on it will be the very setup you're discussing here.\n\nSorry, WO, but for me, this was an absolute no-brainer. See the homepage in the morning for the reasons why, but a clue is that Simon's chart is in the wrong homework section:)\n\nBest\n\nIf\n\nPlease share the link to this No- Brainer trades section. I can't find it using search.","a":"Enlightenme","d":"","n":"#1247","p":50,"im":[],"m":1247},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1248","t":"is this the right CP?","a":"Aek0","d":"","n":"#1248","p":50,"im":["ff42d9c565a1a16e537fa82c8332e0281441804a","3fb254a60ddc3840c046b52cd817faca8bba38c6","d9b266cd70fef4ec4a922ae39d9341764b0a888c"],"m":1248},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1249","t":"Hi guys, I can't seem to check page 1. I have to start with page 2. It would be nice if someone can reach out to the moderators. Hope this gets fix soon.:)","a":"Enlightenme","d":"","n":"#1249","p":50,"im":[],"m":1249},{"id":"aboutcompression_p50_1250","t":"hey guys. i can't chek page 1 too. wish this issue get solved. starting hw from dbr rbd, moving to cp hw. from simple to complex...here are my charts. comments and critiques appreciated\n\n42434445464748495051","a":"Mukhcin","d":"","n":"#1250","p":50,"im":["602755f036c6d583baf034093f6cf241b879ee06","b795892f225b49922d40e7a5639db7b0e094ca75","78ebb6e0b84e87d0d5a202edace5890992264adf","cf50d67cce9d3a7531f975361847c978f28b78f1","a56381c3d8b3cbeb92bbfb79e84c378710b75072"],"m":1250}],"images":[{"k":"991ea1be359743b6730a5d1b458341dd405d7805","t":"assets/thumbs/991ea1be359743b6730a5d1b458341dd405d7805.webp","f":"assets/images/991ea1be359743b6730a5d1b458341dd405d7805.png","w":577,"h":410,"b":60538,"o":"991ea1be359743b6730a5d1b458341dd405d7805.png","p":50,"pid":"aboutcompression_p50_1246"},{"k":"0ae92577e4e9f892d1e08cd818be588fb5658083","t":"assets/thumbs/0ae92577e4e9f892d1e08cd818be588fb5658083.webp","f":"assets/images/0ae92577e4e9f892d1e08cd818be588fb5658083.png","w":1627,"h":654,"b":130215,"o":"0ae92577e4e9f892d1e08cd818be588fb5658083.png","p":50,"pid":"aboutcompression_p50_1226"},{"k":"3a475cdbe89bdbff23c8b7d3e970ca69dd71901d","t":"assets/thumbs/3a475cdbe89bdbff23c8b7d3e970ca69dd71901d.webp","f":"assets/images/3a475cdbe89bdbff23c8b7d3e970ca69dd71901d.png","w":1629,"h":655,"b":155954,"o":"3a475cdbe89bdbff23c8b7d3e970ca69dd71901d.png","p":50,"pid":"aboutcompression_p50_1226"},{"k":"80195818f8c721ee8e548c3d94ba51e72fc9a30c","t":"assets